<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[;; ============================================================
;; Decentralised task allocation vs. central orchestrator
;;
;; The NetLogo world is the 2-D TASK space, not physical space:
;;   x-axis = item weight (0-100), y-axis = fragility (0-100).
;; A robot's position is its tuning centre; "moving" = calibration drift.
;; One tick = one task. Each task is resolved before the next arrives.
;; ============================================================

breed [ agents an-agent ]
breed [ tasks a-task ]

agents-own [
  fit               ;; match to the task being contested: exp(-d^2 / w^2)
  acc               ;; accumulator (evidence for winning the current task)
  new-acc           ;; buffer so all accumulators update simultaneously
  theta             ;; commitment threshold (only ever decreases, to theta-min)
  wins              ;; running tally of tasks won
  wins-first-half   ;; snapshot of wins at half-time (win persistence check)
  active?           ;; still in the current competition?
]

;; NOTE: num-agents, run-seed, theta0, theta-min, xi, eta, leak,
;; inhibition, noise, t-max, centralised? and task-distribution are
;; interface widgets (sliders / switch / chooser), so they are not declared here.
;; w is NOT a slider: it is computed from the pool size in setup.

globals [
  w                                 ;; shared tuning width = 100 * sqrt(4 / (pi * N))
  tasks-per-agent n-tasks
  task-list task-x task-y
  cluster-centres cluster-weights cluster-sd
  n-regions-side
  plot-every                        ;; per-agent win plot is sampled every plot-every tasks

  ;; per-task scratch values, filled by the allocators
  best-fit cur-winner cur-msgs cur-rounds cur-time cur-quality

  ;; running totals for the measures
  total-tasks abstained
  msg-total quality-sum
  rounds-assigned-total time-assigned-total   ;; rounds / decision time, assigned tasks only
  msgs-first msgs-last              ;; message totals in first / last 10% of tasks
  time-first time-last              ;; decision time totals (assigned) in first / last 10%
  assigned-first assigned-last      ;; assigned task counts in first / last 10%
  region-tasks region-abstained     ;; per-region counts (abstention by region)
  assigned-times                    ;; decision times of assigned tasks (for T_max pilot)
]

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; SETUP
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to setup
  clear-all
  resize-world 0 100 0 100
  set-patch-size 4
  random-seed run-seed          ;; same seed => same robots and same task sequence

  set w 100 * sqrt (4 / (pi * num-agents))   ;; ~4 robots within reach of a task (uniform)
  set tasks-per-agent 50        ;; ~50 tasks per robot on average
  set n-tasks tasks-per-agent * num-agents
  set n-regions-side 5          ;; 5 x 5 regions for per-region abstention
  set cluster-weights (list 0.60 0.25 0.15)
  set cluster-sd 8
  set cluster-centres n-values 3 [ (list (random-float 100) (random-float 100)) ]

  setup-agents                  ;; robots and tasks are drawn BEFORE any
  generate-tasks                ;; allocator randomness, so both allocators
                                ;; see identical robots and tasks per seed
  set total-tasks 0
  set abstained 0
  set msg-total 0
  set quality-sum 0
  set rounds-assigned-total 0
  set time-assigned-total 0
  set msgs-first 0
  set msgs-last 0
  set time-first 0
  set time-last 0
  set assigned-first 0
  set assigned-last 0
  set assigned-times []
  set region-tasks n-values (n-regions-side * n-regions-side) [ 0 ]
  set region-abstained n-values (n-regions-side * n-regions-side) [ 0 ]
  reset-ticks
  setup-win-plot
end

to setup-agents
  create-agents num-agents [
    setxy (random-float 100) (random-float 100)   ;; uniform random tuning centre
    set shape "circle"
    set size 2.5
    set color item (who mod 14) base-colors        ;; deterministic, matches its plot line
    set theta theta0                              ;; identical starting threshold
    set acc 0
    set wins 0
    set wins-first-half 0
    set active? false
    pen-down                                      ;; trail = drift of the tuning centre
  ]
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; PER-AGENT WIN TRACKING (one thin line per robot)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to setup-win-plot
  set plot-every max (list 1 (floor (n-tasks / 250)))
  set-current-plot "wins per agent"
  clear-plot
  ask agents [
    create-temporary-plot-pen (word "robot " who)
    set-plot-pen-color color
    plotxy 0 0
  ]
end

to update-win-plot
  if (ticks mod plot-every = 0) or (ticks >= n-tasks) [
    set-current-plot "wins per agent"
    ask agents [
      set-current-plot-pen (word "robot " who)
      plotxy ticks wins
    ]
  ]
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; TASK GENERATION
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to generate-tasks
  set task-list n-values n-tasks [ draw-task ]
end

to-report draw-task
  ifelse task-distribution = "uniform" [
    report (list (random-float 100) (random-float 100))
  ] [
    ;; clustered: three normal clusters (60% / 25% / 15%), sd = 8
    let c pick-cluster
    let cx item 0 (item c cluster-centres)
    let cy item 1 (item c cluster-centres)
    let tx random-normal cx cluster-sd
    let ty random-normal cy cluster-sd
    while [ tx < 0 or tx > 100 or ty < 0 or ty > 100 ] [    ;; redraw if outside the space
      set tx random-normal cx cluster-sd
      set ty random-normal cy cluster-sd
    ]
    report (list tx ty)
  ]
end

to-report pick-cluster
  let r random-float 1
  if r < item 0 cluster-weights [ report 0 ]
  if r < (item 0 cluster-weights) + (item 1 cluster-weights) [ report 1 ]
  report 2
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; MAIN LOOP  (one tick = one task)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to go
  if ticks >= n-tasks [ stop ]
  if ticks = floor (n-tasks / 2) [ ask agents [ set wins-first-half wins ] ]
  next-task
  ifelse centralised?                 ;; switch: on = central orchestrator, off = decentralised
    [ allocate-central ]
    [ allocate-decentralised ]
  record-task
  tick
  update-win-plot
end

to next-task
  ask tasks [ die ]
  let t item ticks task-list
  set task-x item 0 t
  set task-y item 1 t
  create-tasks 1 [
    setxy task-x task-y
    set shape "x"
    set size 3
    set color white
  ]
  ;; highest fitness of ANY robot in the pool (denominator of allocation quality),
  ;; taken before the winner adapts
  let dmin min [ distancexy task-x task-y ] of agents
  set best-fit exp ((0 - (dmin * dmin)) / (w * w))
  set cur-winner nobody
  set cur-msgs 0
  set cur-rounds 0
  set cur-time 0
  set cur-quality 0
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; DECENTRALISED ALLOCATOR (leaky competing accumulator, summed inhibition)
;;   acc(r+1) = max(0, acc + dt*(fit - leak*acc - inhibition*SUM rival acc) + sqrt(dt)*eps)
;;   dt = min(1, 1 / (leak + inhibition*(n - 1))),  n = robots still competing
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to allocate-decentralised
  set cur-msgs 1                    ;; the task announcement on the shared channel

  ;; robots whose tuning width covers the task join the competition
  ;; (if none join, the loop below never runs and the task is abstained immediately)
  let candidates agents with [ (distancexy task-x task-y) <= w ]
  ask candidates [
    let d distancexy task-x task-y
    set fit exp ((0 - (d * d)) / (w * w))     ;; Gaussian tuning curve, fixed for this task
    set acc 0
    set active? true
  ]

  let r 0
  let sim-time 0
  while [ cur-winner = nobody and sim-time < t-max and any? candidates with [ active? ] ] [
    set r r + 1
    let live candidates with [ active? ]
    let n-live count live
    set cur-msgs cur-msgs + n-live            ;; each live robot broadcasts its accumulator once per round
    let total-acc sum [ acc ] of live
    ;; adaptive step size: every competitor computes the same n from the messages it received
    let dt min (list 1 (1 / (leak + inhibition * (n-live - 1))))
    set sim-time sim-time + dt

    ;; simultaneous update: compute all new values first, then apply
    ask live [
      let rival-sum total-acc - acc           ;; inhibition uses the SUM of rivals' accumulators
      set new-acc max (list 0
        (acc + dt * (fit - (leak * acc) - (inhibition * rival-sum))
             + (sqrt dt) * (random-normal 0 noise)))
    ]
    ask live [
      set acc new-acc
      if acc <= 0 [ set active? false ]       ;; dropped out for this task, does not return
    ]

    ;; commit: accumulator reached own threshold; largest margin wins, ties at random
    let reached live with [ active? and acc >= theta ]
    if any? reached [
      let best-margin max [ acc - theta ] of reached
      set cur-winner one-of reached with [ (acc - theta) = best-margin ]
    ]
  ]
  ask candidates [ set active? false ]

  set cur-rounds r
  set cur-time sim-time
  if cur-winner != nobody [
    set cur-quality ([ fit ] of cur-winner) / best-fit
    adapt-winner cur-winner
  ]
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; CENTRAL ORCHESTRATOR (baseline)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to allocate-central
  ;; announcement + N state reports + 1 assignment
  set cur-msgs num-agents + 2
  set cur-rounds 1                            ;; decides in a single step
  set cur-time 1

  ask agents [
    let d distancexy task-x task-y
    set fit exp ((0 - (d * d)) / (w * w))     ;; same fitness function
  ]
  ;; eligible: task within w AND fit high enough to reach theta within t-max
  let eligible agents with [ ((distancexy task-x task-y) <= w) and (fit >= fit-bar theta) ]
  if any? eligible [
    set cur-winner max-one-of eligible [ fit ]
    set cur-quality ([ fit ] of cur-winner) / best-fit
    adapt-winner cur-winner
  ]
end

;; fitness at which a rival-free accumulator (n = 1, so dt = 1) reaches th within t-max rounds:
;; fit >= th * leak / (1 - (1 - leak)^t-max)
to-report fit-bar [ th ]
  report th * leak / (1 - ((1 - leak) ^ t-max))
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; ADAPTATION (identical for both allocators; winner only)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to adapt-winner [ a ]
  ask a [
    ;; tuning centre moves a fraction eta of the way toward the task (SOM update, no neighbourhood)
    set xcor xcor + eta * (task-x - xcor)
    set ycor ycor + eta * (task-y - ycor)
    ;; threshold drops by xi, down to theta-min
    set theta max (list theta-min (theta - xi))
    set wins wins + 1
  ]
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; BOOKKEEPING
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to record-task
  set total-tasks total-tasks + 1
  set msg-total msg-total + cur-msgs
  let in-first? ticks < n-first
  let in-last? ticks >= n-tasks - n-first
  if in-first? [ set msgs-first msgs-first + cur-msgs ]
  if in-last?  [ set msgs-last msgs-last + cur-msgs ]

  let reg region-of task-x task-y
  set region-tasks replace-item reg region-tasks ((item reg region-tasks) + 1)
  ifelse cur-winner = nobody [
    set abstained abstained + 1
    set region-abstained replace-item reg region-abstained ((item reg region-abstained) + 1)
  ] [
    ;; rounds and decision time are measured on assigned tasks only
    set quality-sum quality-sum + cur-quality
    set rounds-assigned-total rounds-assigned-total + cur-rounds
    set time-assigned-total time-assigned-total + cur-time
    set assigned-times fput cur-time assigned-times
    if in-first? [ set time-first time-first + cur-time  set assigned-first assigned-first + 1 ]
    if in-last?  [ set time-last time-last + cur-time    set assigned-last assigned-last + 1 ]
  ]
end

to-report region-of [ x y ]
  let side 100 / n-regions-side
  let cx min (list (n-regions-side - 1) (floor (x / side)))
  let cy min (list (n-regions-side - 1) (floor (y / side)))
  report cx + (n-regions-side * cy)
end

to-report n-first                       ;; size of the "first / last 10%" windows
  report ceiling (0.1 * n-tasks)
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; T-MAX PILOT: run the decentralised allocator with a generous limit,
;; then set t-max to the 95th percentile of SIMULATED TIME (sum of dt) until commitment.
;; Set num-agents / task-distribution first, then press the button.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to calibrate-t-max
  set centralised? false
  set t-max 500
  setup
  repeat floor (n-tasks / 5) [ go ]                ;; pilot = 10 tasks per robot
  let sorted sort assigned-times
  ifelse empty? sorted [
    user-message "Pilot found no assigned tasks; t-max left at 500."
  ] [
    let p95 item (floor (0.95 * ((length sorted) - 1))) sorted
    set t-max max (list 1 (precision p95 1))
    print (word "Pilot: t-max set to " t-max " (95th percentile of simulated time to commitment)")
  ]
  setup
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------
;; MEASURES  (monitors / BehaviorSpace)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------
to-report comm-per-task                 ;; messages per task (all tasks)
  ifelse total-tasks = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report msg-total / total-tasks ]
end

to-report mean-allocation-quality       ;; winner fitness / best fitness in pool (assigned tasks only)
  let assigned total-tasks - abstained
  ifelse assigned = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report quality-sum / assigned ]
end

to-report rounds-per-task               ;; rounds until commitment, assigned tasks only
  let assigned total-tasks - abstained
  ifelse assigned = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report rounds-assigned-total / assigned ]
end

to-report decision-time                 ;; simulated time (sum of dt) until commitment, assigned only
  let assigned total-tasks - abstained
  ifelse assigned = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report time-assigned-total / assigned ]
end

to-report abstain-rate
  ifelse total-tasks = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report abstained / total-tasks ]
end

to-report region-abstain-rates          ;; abstention rate per region (0 where no tasks arrived)
  report (map [ [t a] -> ifelse-value (t = 0) [ 0 ] [ a / t ] ] region-tasks region-abstained)
end

to-report max-region-abstain-rate       ;; worst-served region that received tasks
  let rates []
  (foreach region-tasks region-abstained [ [t a] ->
    if t > 0 [ set rates lput (a / t) rates ]
  ])
  ifelse empty? rates [ report 0 ] [ report max rates ]
end

to-report win-gini                      ;; Gini coefficient of win counts across robots
  let xs sort [ wins ] of agents
  let n length xs
  let s sum xs
  if s = 0 [ report 0 ]
  let weighted 0
  let i 1
  foreach xs [ x ->
    set weighted weighted + (i * x)
    set i i + 1
  ]
  report ((2 * weighted) / (n * s)) - ((n + 1) / n)
end

to-report wins-by-agent                 ;; win count of every robot, ordered by who number
  report map [ a -> [ wins ] of a ] sort agents
end

to-report messages-per-task-first10     ;; H2: communication cost early in the run
  let n min (list total-tasks n-first)
  ifelse n = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report msgs-first / n ]
end

to-report messages-per-task-last10      ;; H2: communication cost late in the run
  let n max (list 0 (total-tasks - (n-tasks - n-first)))
  ifelse n = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report msgs-last / n ]
end

to-report decision-time-first10         ;; H2: decision time early in the run (assigned only)
  ifelse assigned-first = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report time-first / assigned-first ]
end

to-report decision-time-last10          ;; H2: decision time late in the run (assigned only)
  ifelse assigned-last = 0 [ report 0 ] [ report time-last / assigned-last ]
end

to-report early-late-win-correlation    ;; do first-half winners keep winning? (H3)
  let xs [ wins-first-half ] of agents
  let ys [ wins - wins-first-half ] of agents
  let sx standard-deviation xs
  let sy standard-deviation ys
  if sx = 0 or sy = 0 [ report 0 ]
  let mx mean xs
  let my mean ys
  report (sum (map [ [a b] -> (a - mx) * (b - my) ] xs ys)) / (((length xs) - 1) * sx * sy)
end
]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="368" wrappingAllowedX="false" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="0" height="408" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="4.0" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="false" width="408" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="100" updateMode="0" maxPxcor="100" minPxcor="0"></view>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="10" max="200" width="170" display="num-agents" height="50" min="5" direction="Horizontal" default="200.0" variable="num-agents"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="60" max="1000" width="170" display="run-seed" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="run-seed"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="0.1" y="110" max="10" width="170" display="theta0" height="50" min="0.5" direction="Horizontal" default="3.0" variable="theta0"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="0.1" y="160" max="10" width="170" display="theta-min" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="theta-min"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="0.1" y="210" max="1000" width="170" display="t-max" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="50.0" variable="t-max"></slider>
    <slider x="190" step="0.01" y="10" max="1" width="170" display="leak" height="50" min="0.01" direction="Horizontal" default="0.2" variable="leak"></slider>
    <slider x="190" step="0.01" y="60" max="1" width="170" display="inhibition" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.3" variable="inhibition"></slider>
    <slider x="190" step="0.01" y="110" max="1" width="170" display="noise" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.05" variable="noise"></slider>
    <slider x="190" step="0.01" y="160" max="1" width="170" display="eta" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.1" variable="eta"></slider>
    <slider x="190" step="0.01" y="210" max="2" width="170" display="xi" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.05" variable="xi"></slider>
    <switch x="10" y="265" height="45" on="true" variable="centralised?" width="170" display="centralised?"></switch>
    <chooser x="190" y="265" height="60" variable="task-distribution" current="1" width="170" display="task-distribution">
      <choice type="string" value="uniform"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="clustered"></choice>
    </chooser>
    <button x="10" y="330" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="80" display="setup">setup</button>
    <button x="100" y="330" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="80" display="go">go</button>
    <button x="190" y="330" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="170" display="calibrate t-max">calibrate-t-max</button>
    <plot x="10" autoPlotX="true" yMax="10.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="wins" y="380" xMin="0.0" height="260" legend="false" xMax="100.0" yMin="0.0" width="350" xAxis="tasks" display="wins per agent">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
    </plot>
    <monitor x="368" precision="0" y="430" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="tasks done">total-tasks</monitor>
    <monitor x="503" precision="3" y="430" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="abstain rate">abstain-rate</monitor>
    <monitor x="638" precision="3" y="430" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="allocation quality">mean-allocation-quality</monitor>
    <monitor x="368" precision="2" y="480" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="messages / task">comm-per-task</monitor>
    <monitor x="503" precision="2" y="480" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="rounds / task">rounds-per-task</monitor>
    <monitor x="638" precision="3" y="480" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="win Gini">win-gini</monitor>
    <monitor x="368" precision="3" y="530" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="max region abstain">max-region-abstain-rate</monitor>
    <monitor x="503" precision="2" y="530" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="msgs/task first 10%">messages-per-task-first10</monitor>
    <monitor x="638" precision="2" y="530" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="msgs/task last 10%">messages-per-task-last10</monitor>
    <monitor x="503" precision="2" y="580" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="decision time">decision-time</monitor>
    <monitor x="638" precision="2" y="580" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="width w">w</monitor>
    <monitor x="368" precision="2" y="630" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="dec. time first 10%">decision-time-first10</monitor>
    <monitor x="503" precision="2" y="630" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="dec. time last 10%">decision-time-last10</monitor>
    <monitor x="368" precision="3" y="580" height="60" fontSize="11" width="125" display="mode">ifelse-value centralised? [ "centralised" ] [ "decentralised" ]</monitor>
  </widgets>
  <info>## WHAT IS IT?

A decentralised task allocator for a warehouse of picking robots, compared with a central orchestrator. The world is the 2-D task space (x = item weight, y = fragility, both 0-100), not physical space. A robot's position is its tuning centre; moving means its calibration drifting.

## HOW IT WORKS

One tick = one task. Decentralised: robots whose width w covers the task compete in rounds. acc = max(0, acc + dt*(fit - leak*acc - inhibition*SUM(rival acc)) + sqrt(dt)*noise), with dt = min(1, 1/(leak + inhibition*(n-1))). w = 100*sqrt(4/(pi*N)) so about 4 robots reach each task. A robot commits when acc reaches its threshold; the winner's centre moves a fraction eta toward the task and its threshold drops by xi (floor theta-min). If nobody commits before the simulated time (sum of dt) reaches t-max the task is abstained. Centralised mode (orchestrator): picks the eligible robot with the highest fitness (eligible = within w and able to reach its threshold within t-max rounds) using N + 2 messages, and adapts the winner identically.

## HOW TO USE IT

Use the centralised? switch (off = decentralised, on = central orchestrator) and the task-distribution chooser, set num-agents and run-seed, press setup, then go. The run stops after 50 x num-agents tasks. calibrate-t-max runs a pilot and sets t-max to the 95th percentile of simulated time to commitment. The 'wins per agent' plot draws one thin line per robot (same colour as the robot and its drift trail in the view). The BehaviorSpace experiment main-comparison covers 2 allocators x 2 distributions x 4 pool sizes x 20 seeds. The same seed gives both allocators the same robots and task sequence.

## MEASURES

messages per task, allocation quality (winner fit / best fit), rounds per task and decision time (assigned tasks only), abstain rate (overall and per region), win Gini, first vs last 10% messages, early/late win correlation.

## NOTE

Defaults follow Table 1 (leak 0.2, inhibition 0.3, noise 0.05, theta0 3, theta-min 1, xi 0.05, eta 0.1). t-max is a placeholder until set with calibrate-t-max.
</info>
